Day 1: Type System & Memory Architecture

Value types vs. reference types, stack vs. heap allocation, struct vs. class, ref struct, nullability mechanics (Nullable<T>, nullable reference types, compiler checks vs. runtime nulls).

Day 2: Object-Oriented Semantics & Modern Pattern Matching

Inheritance vs. composition, virtual/override vs. new, abstract classes vs. interfaces, records (record class vs. record struct), switch expressions, property and relational pattern matching.

Day 3: Generics, Collections & Delegates

Generic constraints (where T : class, new()), variance (in/out), collection internals (List<T>, Dictionary<TKey, TValue> hash collisions/growth factors), delegates, Func<T>, Action<T>, lambda expressions.

Day 4: Memory Optimization & Modern Types

Span<T>, ReadOnlySpan<T>, Memory<T>, string allocation overhead, ArrayPool<T>, in/out/ref parameters, unmanaged memory pointers (unsafe context overview).

Day 5: Garbage Collection & Resource Lifetime

Generations 0, 1, and 2, Large Object Heap (LOH), Ephemeral segment, GC triggers and compaction, IDisposable, IAsyncDisposable, the standard dispose pattern, SafeHandle.

ay 6: LINQ Architecture & Deferred Execution

IEnumerable<T> vs. IQueryable<T>, extension methods, deferred execution pitfalls (multiple enumeration, closure captures), custom LINQ query operators.


